{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"═══ MEASURED, POST-`afeb`, AGAINST THE REAL API. The floor is 1024, not 4096 — and the prefix\ntoday lands just under it. ═══\n\nThree measurements, all from real `anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6` calls, not from reading code.\n\n**1. THE PREFIX IS GENUINELY RE-SENT PER CALL (observed, not inferred).** A recording proxy runner\nwrapped the real runner around `overlap.judge.judge()` over a 6-candidate corpus of REAL digests\n(produced by `rebar.llm.enrich` on 7 live tickets). 12 calls (6 candidates x 2 orderings):\n\n    distinct system prompts                                   1  (byte-identical, 377 tokens)\n    calls whose USER message contains the query digest block  12 / 12   <- re-sent every time\n    query digest block                                        308 tokens\n    mean instructions (FIRST + SECOND + scaffolding)          608 tokens\n    total input                                        16,040 tokens   (per call 1,273-1,420)\n    cache_read_tokens                                         0\n    cache_write_tokens                                        0\n    model actually invoked                 anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6   (afeb has landed)\n    wall clock                                             25.1 s (sequential, as documented)\n\n**2. THE ACTUAL CACHE FLOOR FOR THE `standard` CLASS IS 1024, NOT 4096.** Direct probe against the\nreal API: a system block with `cache_control: ephemeral`, called twice, at increasing sizes.\n\n    system tokens   call 1 (write / read)   call 2 (write / read)\n      622               0 / 0                  0 / 0\n      922               0 / 0                  0 / 0\n     1042            1035 / 0                  0 / 1035     <- writes and reads\n     1117            1110 / 0                  0 / 1110\n     4222            4215 / 0                  0 / 4215\n\nSo the repo's `CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS = 4096` (`llm/capabilities.py:330`, documented as the \"Opus\n4.8 floor\") does NOT describe the model `overlap-judge` runs on post-`afeb`. The applicable floor is\n**1024**. This resolves the crux this ticket named, in the favourable direction — 4096 would have\nmade the design dead on arrival.\n\n**3. THE PROPOSED PREFIX IS MARGINAL AGAINST THAT FLOOR, AND THAT IS THE HONEST RISK.** `system +\nFIRST` = 377 + 308 ~= 685 tokens of *text*. But the billed prefix ahead of the cache breakpoint also\ncarries the structured-output tool surface: measured per-call input is 1,324 while system +\ninstructions is only 985, so ~339 tokens of tool/scaffold sit in front. Prefix after the move is\ntherefore ~1,024 +/- the digest's own size — straddling the floor rather than clearly over it. The\nearlier estimate of ~800 tokens per digest was arithmetic; measured digests are 241-362 tokens, so\nthe prefix is smaller than that estimate predicted.\n\nCONSEQUENCE, stated up front rather than discovered later: the move is **never worse** (identical\nbytes, just relocated from the user block to the cacheable system block) but its saving is\nCONDITIONAL on the prefix clearing 1024 for the ticket being reviewed. The implementation therefore\nships the relocation and the ticket records the measured after-numbers honestly, including a zero if\nthat is what the corpus produces.\n\n**NOT PARALLELIZING.** The loop is sequential (`judge.py`, a plain `for cand in candidates:`), so the\nfirst call writes the prefix and the rest read it — the warm-before-fan-out requirement recorded on\nthis ticket binds only if the loop is parallelized, and this change does not parallelize it. Left\nalone deliberately: fanning out cold calls that share a prefix would turn 1 write + N-1 reads into N\npremium writes, which is the regression that requirement exists to prevent.\n\n**NO CHILDREN.** The chosen option is a single relocation inside one function in one file plus its\ntests. Decomposing it would create children smaller than the 100-LOC floor with no independent\nreview value."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785706468187978001,"uuid":"a707034f-c012-47b4-bf87-e3e16df434d8"}